invariant: INV-16
file: sha256_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha2-equiv
reason: sha256_hw.c's first round constant is one more than FIPS 180-4
  §4.2.2's, so every digest a session computes on the instructions is
  wrong, and it agrees with no peer and with none of this tree's own
  portable digests. CBMC cannot read an intrinsic, so no proof covers this
  file, and bin/sha2_equiv_test is what holds it to sha256.c. The table
  sits outside the two architecture arms, so the x86-64 build the script
  runs under qemu-x86_64 holds it for arm64 too. A machine's own CPU may
  lack the instructions, where the binary skips, so the catch is the
  script: qemu's max model has them on every host. The lane skips without
  docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

